        "original_id": "42f4cfe0-d3bd-53ff-be3e-6bb5cbaf1dfb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Keri Hulme, Orson Scott Card\n- Works: The Bone People, Ender's Game, Speaker for the Dead\n- Awards: Booker Prize, Hugo Award, Nebula Award\n\nFacts:\n- In 1985, Keri Hulme's only novel, \"The Bone People,\" won the Booker Prize.\n- In 1985, Orson Scott Card's novel \"Ender's Game\" won both the Hugo Award and the Nebula Award.\n- In 1986, Orson Scott Card's sequel \"Speaker for the Dead\" won both the Hugo Award and the Nebula Award.\n- Orson Scott Card became the only author to win both the Hugo Award and the Nebula Award in consecutive years.",
